{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> Because Sihon defeated Moab, it says in the Book of the Wars of HaShem — like in the chronicles, in which they write the wars between nation and nation, and the victories that the Holy One, blessed be He, gives to one nation against its fellow — and written in it is the matter of the king of Moab." "<b>Ethe-vav-heh-beh at its end.</b> את והב is one word, and it is like בהתודע יוסף which is interpreted as באתודע, and so too here את והב is like אתיהב — was given to the king of Moab at its end, and in the storm, which is a defeat, for his land was taken up to the wadi."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The note reads את והב as equivalent to אתיהב ('was given'), drawing an analogy with בהתודע/באתודע. The reconstruction relies on unvocalized medieval orthography; the comparison word בהתודע יוסף is itself obscure and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:45.488941514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}